# Rust build artifacts
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Everything `emberly init` and a running session materialize in this repo:
# transcripts, per-session scratch space (FR-8, T-17), project memory, and the
# local config.toml carrying a personal provider/model choice. All of it is
# developer-local dogfooding output, so the whole directory is ignored rather
# than enumerated — a new session artifact should not silently appear in
# `git status`.
#
# This is also why glob/grep do not surface scratch content by default: both
# honor .gitignore (Tech Spec §8.3).
#
# Note this is emberly-code's own choice. `emberly init` treats
# .agents/config.toml as shareable, and another project may well want to commit
# it; nothing here changes that.
.agents/

# Local secrets — never committed (Tech Spec §8)
keys.toml

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
